        "text": "Summary\nYou\u2019ve just finished another great chapter in this book! This post-exploitation\nchapter should have given you another perspective of the penetration testing\ntechniques. Remember that you can dump credentials from a Windows host\n(and a Linux host too) to reuse them somewhere else. You could log in to another\nsystem like a SQL database or another host\u2019s shared folder, SSH, FTP, email,\nintranet portal, etc.\nAfter that, you learned how to pivot using local, remote, and dynamic port\nforwarding over SSH.\nIn the next chapter, you will see how to crack hashes, including the NTLM\nhash. More fun to come!",
